A .ssl script whose content is a one-line SQL statement. SQL-mode
classification is scoped to data sources (feature.diagnostics_pipeline
A12, feature.formatting A11), so this stays SSL: it is formatted as SSL
(a terminating `;` is added) and the SSL checks run and report on the SQL
syntax. The flag variants run the same content under `--ds`, which
declares any input a data source (feature.cli_contract A15): then it is
SQL, passes through unchanged and reports nothing. Kept to one line: a
multi-line SQL body in a .ssl file trips the "formatting introduces no
new error" invariant (each line gains a `;` and becomes its own
unexpected_token statement), reported separately.
-- input.ssl --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU'
-- format [--ds] --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU'
-- diagnostics [--ds] --
-- format --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU';
-- diagnostics --
1:8-1:9 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'v' - expected an operator or ';'
1:9-1:19 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:vendor_id' instead of 'object.vendor_id'
1:41-1:48 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:active' instead of 'object.active'
1:55-1:58 error bare_logical_operator: Use '.AND.' instead of 'and' for logical operations in SSL
1:60-1:67 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:region' instead of 'object.region'
